      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant_City%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1860, Plant City was briefly renamed Cork, after the postmaster's Irish hometown, before adopting its current name in honor of Henry B. Plant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant_City%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Plant City was incorporated on January 10, 1885, significantly boosting commerce in this primarily agricultural community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant_City%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Cincinnati Reds used to hold their spring training in Plant City, playing exhibition games at Plant City Stadium from 1988 to 1997.",
